  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, Office of Enforcement and Compliance Assurance (OECA): Support for Secretariat of the International Network for Environmental Complinace and Enforcement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds go towards two activities: 1.) Cooperative Agreement with the Institute for Governance &amp; Sustainable Development (IGSD) to provide Secretariat support for the International Network for Environmental Compliance and Enforcement (INECE). EPA provides support to INECE for the development of effective enforcement programs in other countries to improve the rule of law and good governance internationally, in order to better control global pollution that can effect the U.S. and provide a level playing field for U.S. companies competing in world trade. 2.) Cooperative Agreement with IGSD to support the Seaport Environmental Security Network (SESN) to enhance the ability of the worlds ports to stop illegal shipments of hazardous waste. For more information on INECE or SESN, visit: www.inece.org.</narrative>
  </description>
